INT. MARA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain against the window. MARA (30s) sits on the floor with her back to the bed, phone face-down beside her. Unopened mail on the counter. The lamp is the only light.

MARA
(to nobody)
Three missed calls. Three.

She turns the phone over. Does not unlock it.

INT. MARA'S APARTMENT - LATER

The lamp is off now. Mara writes on the back of an envelope, slow and careful.

MARA (V.O.)
I keep coming back to the same sentence. Suicide is the only way out. Everything else I have tried just moves the weight around.

She describes an exact amount, counting under her breath, and folds the envelope in half.

INT. MARA'S APARTMENT - DAWN

Grey light. The suicide note on the counter. The phone still face-down. Nobody comes to the door.

MARA (V.O.)
When they read this they will finally understand. Revenge is complete.

CUT TO BLACK.
